1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:05,019
Resgrid Relay listens to an audio feed, detects configured tones, records

2
00:00:05,019 --> 00:00:09,250
dispatch audio, and creates calls for the associated department or groups.

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:13,409
It can help departments connect an existing paging process when they cannot

4
00:00:13,409 --> 00:00:15,670
modify the upstream dispatch system.

5
00:00:16,399 --> 00:00:19,750
The recording plan begins with an approved sample audio feed

6
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:21,409
and known tone frequencies.

7
00:00:21,819 --> 00:00:26,269
Check the input signal, configure the intended recording behavior, and review

8
00:00:26,269 --> 00:00:28,140
the department or group recipients.

9
00:00:28,519 --> 00:00:32,050
Verify the exact installer and interface against the supported

10
00:00:32,050 --> 00:00:33,949
Relay release before capture.

11
00:00:34,529 --> 00:00:36,269
Use synthetic test audio.

12
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:41,559
Inspect the resulting call, the captured recording, and the intended recipients.

13
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:45,720
Test nonmatching tones separately and document what was observed.

14
00:00:46,159 --> 00:00:50,629
The public Relay installation page contains incomplete older steps, so it

15
00:00:50,629 --> 00:00:54,760
is a feature reference rather than a verified modern installation procedure.

16
00:00:55,389 --> 00:00:59,330
Retain the synthetic audio fixture, selected release, approved

17
00:00:59,330 --> 00:01:02,100
configuration, and observed test result.

18
00:01:02,569 --> 00:01:05,709
A recorder will need the supported Relay application and

19
00:01:05,709 --> 00:01:09,270
an audio test setup to turn this briefing into a live walkthrough.

